---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import { buttonClass, demoClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';
---
<MotionPage title="Motion: scroll" description="scrollTo moves an element into place over a spring, and follows a layout that moves while it runs.">
  <h1>Scroll</h1>
  <p><code>scrollTo(target, &#123; container, timing, offset, focus &#125;)</code>, from <code>@udixio/motion/scroll</code>, scrolls an element into place over a spring. The target is an element or a <code>&#123; x, y &#125;</code> position. By default the nearest scrollable ancestor of the element scrolls, or the page; <code>container</code> names another scroller.</p>

  <h2>Use</h2>
  <pre><code>{`import { scrollTo } from '@udixio/motion/scroll';

const { finished } = scrollTo(document.getElementById('pricing')!, { focus: true });
await finished; // 'finished' at the destination, or 'cancelled' when the user scrolled`}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li>The start edge of the element is brought to the start of the visible area, past the <code>scroll-padding</code> of the scroller and the <code>scroll-margin</code> of the element.</li>
    <li><code>offset</code> adds pixels to the destination, in scroll units.</li>
    <li>The spring is <code>spring.slow.spatial</code> unless <code>timing</code> says otherwise. The destination is read on each frame, so the scroll follows a layout that moves while it runs.</li>
    <li><code>focus: true</code> gives the focus to the target on arrival, without scrolling again. A target that cannot take focus gets <code>tabindex="-1"</code>.</li>
    <li><code>scrollDestination(target, options)</code> reads where the same scroll would stop, without scrolling.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The scroll returns <code>&#123; finished, cancel() &#125;</code>. <code>finished</code> resolves to <code>'finished'</code> at the destination, or <code>'cancelled'</code>. A wheel turn, a touch, a pointer press or a key press of the user cancels it, and so does a new scroll of the same container. While it runs, the <code>overflow-anchor</code> of the scroller is <code>none</code>, and it is given back at the end.</p>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>The box below scrolls its own content. The button scrolls the box to the target at its end, and gives the target focus.</p>
  <div class={demoClass}>
    <button type="button" class={buttonClass} data-scroll-go>Scroll to the target</button>
    <div id="scroll-box" class="h-40 w-full overflow-y-auto rounded-2xl bg-surface-container p-4 text-body-large text-on-surface">
      <p class="mb-40">Scroll down: the target is below.</p>
      <p id="scroll-target" tabindex="-1" class="rounded-xl bg-surface-container-high p-3">Target</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, the scroll jumps to its destination.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Scroll anchoring is off on the scroller while the scroll runs.</li>
  </ul>

  <script>
    import { scrollTo } from '@udixio/motion/scroll';

    document.addEventListener('click', event => {
      if (!(event.target instanceof Element)) return;
      if (!event.target.closest('[data-scroll-go]')) return;
      const box = document.getElementById('scroll-box');
      const target = document.getElementById('scroll-target');
      if (box && target) scrollTo(target, { container: box, focus: true });
    });
  </script>
</MotionPage>
